course: dictionary
lesson: 12090
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word clutches can mean holding something tightly, or it can mean a group of eggs. The sentence around it tells you which meaning to use. «She clutches her teddy when the thunder starts.» Here clutches is a verb: she is holding her teddy tightly because she is scared.
explain: «The bird sat on her clutch of eggs all spring.» Here clutch is a set of eggs laid at one time, and clutches is the plural: more than one set. Ask yourself: is someone doing an action, or is this a group of things? That question helps you choose the right meaning.
explain: «The hero escaped from the clutches of the wicked villain.» Here clutches means the power or control of someone dangerous. "In the clutches of" is a phrase meaning trapped by someone. Phrases like this are easier to learn as a whole than word by word.
explain: Context can also show a machine. «Sam pressed the clutch and the car moved off.» A clutch is a pedal in a car. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
fact: «Clutches» is the plural of «clutch», and it is also the verb form that means holding something tightly.
fact: «In the clutches of» means in the power or control of someone dangerous.
fact: «Clutch» can mean a set of eggs laid at one time, a pedal in a car, or a small handbag with no handles.
fact: «Clutches at straws» means trying anything, even if it is hopeless.
fact: Check the sentence: is someone holding something, or is it a group, a power, or a machine? That tells you the meaning.
exercise: «The little girl clutches her teddy bear during the storm.» What does clutches mean here? | Lays eggs in a nest | Escapes from danger | Presses a pedal in a car | *Holds something tightly
exercise: «The bird sat on her clutch of eggs.» What does clutch mean here? | A small handbag with no handles | *A set of eggs laid at one time | A tight hold on something | A pedal in a car
exercise: «The prince was saved from the clutches of the wicked witch.» What does clutches mean here? | Holding something tightly because of fear | *The power or control of someone dangerous | Sets of eggs | Small handbags
test: «Dad pressed the clutch and the car moved off.» What is the clutch in this sentence? | A tight hold on something | A group of eggs | *A pedal that connects the engine to the wheels | A small bag with no handles
test: Ellie says the phrase «clutches at straws» means she is very lucky. What does it really mean? | Holding a bunch of straw tightly | *Trying anything, even if it is hopeless | Winning every game | Finding the right answer at once
exam: «Mia clutched the rail as the boat rocked.» What does clutched mean here? | Laid eggs in a nest | Escaped from danger | *Held tightly | Pressed a pedal in a car
